<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ven</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hven</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ven is a small island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oresund">Øresund</a> between Zealand and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scania">Scania</a>, part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> since the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-roskilde">Treaty of Roskilde</a> of 1658. In 1576 King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii-of-denmark">Frederick II of Denmark</a> granted it to the astronomer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tycho-brahe">Tycho Brahe</a>, who built the observatories of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uraniborg">Uraniborg</a> and Stjerneborg there and made precise observations of the stars and planets until he left in 1597.</p></div>
